{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall eat old, stored produce.</b> The meaning is that the produce will not spoil and will not become rotten or ruined from long storage, but on the contrary you will choose to eat the older produce — and this is what He means by the doubling <b>יָשָׁן נוֹשָׁן</b>." "And His saying <b>and old from before new you shall bring out</b> means: you will not bring it out to the side where it has grown old and spoiled, but rather on account of the new you shall bring it out. And the reason He wrote this here and not in its proper place above, when He mentioned the blessing of the produce and the blessing of the land, is that the verse intends here to magnify the goodness: that even though it will fruit and multiply for them abundantly, nevertheless they will also have the surpassing goodness of eating old stored produce and so forth — which is not so much the case when the consumers are few, for then even from the little they would eat old stored produce."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:01:48.087936817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}